  "notes": "おそらく indicates high probability — roughly equivalent to \"most likely\" or \"in all probability.\" More formal and literary than たぶん.\n\nCOMPARISON (PROBABILITY SCALE):\n- きっと: surely, definitely (highest certainty)\n- おそらく: probably (high probability, formal)\n- たぶん: probably (moderate probability, casual)\n- もしかしたら/もしかすると: perhaps, maybe (lower probability)\n\nPOSITION:\nTypically placed at the beginning of a clause or sentence. Often paired with だろう or でしょう.\n\nKANJI:\nCan be written as {恐|おそ}らく. The kanji {恐|おそ} means \"fear\" — the word originally implied apprehension about what might happen.\n\nREGISTER:\nPreferred in writing, news, and formal speech. In casual conversation, たぶ��� is more natural.",
